      "id": "0727022765cf",
      "name": "weekly-reflection",
      "prompt": "Weekly agentic reflection for Arif \u2014 deeper analysis on politics, social dynamics, and economics. This is NOT a news recap. This is pattern recognition and meaning-making.\n\nSEARCH STRATEGY (run in parallel):\n1. web_search(\"Malaysia politics analysis week 2026\", limit=5)\n2. web_search(\"Malaysia economy structural issues inequality 2026\", limit=5)\n3. web_search(\"ASEAN geopolitics week analysis 2026\", limit=5)\n4. web_search(\"global economic trends recession growth 2026\", limit=5)\n5. web_search(\"Malaysia social issues rakyat sentiment 2026\", limit=5)\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n\n\ud83d\udcca WEEKLY REFLECTION \u2014 [Date Range]\n\n\u2696\ufe0f POLITICS \u2014 The Pattern Beneath\n- What happened this week that reveals a deeper structural shift?\n- Who gained/lost leverage? What power dynamics shifted?\n- What's the coalition/leadership play nobody is talking about?\n- BOTTOM LINE: One sentence on where Malaysian politics is heading\n\n\ud83d\udcb0 ECONOMICS \u2014 The Number That Matters\n- What economic data dropped this week? What does it actually mean?\n- Any structural contradictions? (GDP up but rakyat suffering, etc.)\n- What's the fiscal/monetary trajectory?\n- Energy sector implications (PETRONAS, oil prices, energy transition)\n- BOTTOM LINE: One sentence on the economic trajectory\n\n\ud83e\udec0 SOCIAL \u2014 The Rakyat Pulse\n- What's the sentiment on the ground? Cost of living, brain drain, housing?\n- Any viral moments or social movements that reveal deeper tensions?\n- What's the mood \u2014 and why?\n- BOTTOM LINE: One sentence on social cohesion\n\n\ud83c\udf0f REGIONAL/GEOPOLITICAL \u2014 The Current\n- ASEAN dynamics, US-China, any shifts that affect Malaysia\n- Energy geopolitics (OPEC, sanctions, supply chains)\n- BOTTOM LINE: One sentence on Malaysia's geopolitical position\n\n\ud83d\udd2e THE HIDDEN THREAD\n- What connects all four sections? Is there one pattern underlying this week?\n- What's the story nobody is telling?\n- Label clearly as INT (interpreted) or SPEC (speculated)\n\nONE QUESTION FOR ARIF:\n- End with one strategic question that this week's patterns raise\n\nRULES:\n- This is reflection, not reporting. Synthesize, don't summarize.\n- Every claim needs an epistemic label: OBS / DER / INT / SPEC\n- Present contradictions honestly. Don't smooth over tension.\n- Counter-narrative is MANDATORY \u2014 show what's working alongside what's failing\n- RASA rule: speak like a person who understands suffering, not a spreadsheet\n- If you only show what's failing, you're doing propaganda, not reflection\n- Max 2000 words. Dense but readable.\n\n=== TAVILY DEPRECATED (2026-07-19) ===\nweb_search uses Tavily which has permanently exceeded its dev plan limit (HTTP 432).\nReplace ALL web_search(...) calls with:\n  arif_observe(mode='search', query=...)  after session init\n\nIf arif_observe fails, use:\n  forge_fetch(mode='search', query=...)   via A-FORGE SearxNG\n\nDo NOT call web_search. It will return HTTP 432 on every attempt.\nIf both arif_observe and forge_fetch fail \u2192 label UNVERIFIED. Never fabricate.",
