      "prompt": "Run a weekly entropy audit on the arifOS kernel repo at /root/arifOS and report findings.\n\n1. Check for new stale branches (merged but not deleted):\n   git branch --merged main | grep -v \"main\\|*\" | head -10\n\n2. Check for large files that may have been added:\n   find /root/arifOS -type f -size +5M -not -path \"*/.git/*\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" | head -10\n\n3. Check git repo size:\n   du -sh /root/arifOS/.git 2>/dev/null\n   git count-objects -vH 2>/dev/null | head -5\n\n4. Check for uncommitted changes:\n   cd /root/arifOS && git status -s | head -10\n\n5. Check surface gate:\n   cd /root/arifOS && make surface-gate 2>&1 | tail -3\n\n6. Check organ health:\n   for svc in arifOS:8088 A-FORGE:7071 AAA:3001 GEOX:8081 WEALTH:18082 WELL:18083; do\n     name=\"${svc%%:*}\"; port=\"${svc##*:}\"\n     curl -sf \"http://127.0.0.1:$port/health\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"  \u2705 $name\" || echo \"  \u274c $name\"\n   done\n\n7. Disk usage trend:\n   df -h / | tail -1\n\nSummarise findings in 3 sections: CRITICAL (needs action), WARN (monitor), INFO (just facts). If everything is clean, say \"\u2705 Zero entropy detected \u2014 kernel clean.\"",
